    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulsĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		mulsum, v. mulceo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sweetened with honey; sweet as honey</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulsea aqua,</span>”
				<i>honey-water, hydromel</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 7, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 19, 75, § 129</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquor mulsei saporis,</span>”
				<i>sweet as honey</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 45, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
